    "['ipv6 unicast-routing', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-options rib inet6.0 static', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set routing-options rib inet6.0 static', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `ipv6 unicast-routing` command:\\n\\n##\\nset routing-options rib inet6.0 static\\n##\\n\\nNote: While this achieves similar functionality, there are some conceptual differences:\\n1. Juniper enables IPv6 routing by default when IPv6 addresses are configured\\n2. The `rib inet6.0 static` command explicitly ensures the IPv6 routing table is created and available for static routes\\n3. For dynamic routing protocols, you would configure them separately in Juniper\\n\\nThe equivalent could also be simply enabling an IPv6 routing protocol, but the above is the most direct functional equivalent to Cisco's global IPv6 unicast routing command.\", 'trans_template': 'set routing-options rib inet6.0 static'}]]": 1,
    "['interface [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [0, 0], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'unit [parameter2] disable', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'disable', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]'}]]": 3,
